#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Kuro OS — Welcome / control centre (GTK4 + libadwaita, Kuro styling).

  bapirlo-welcome           open it
  bapirlo-welcome --daily   what the login autostart runs: opens only on the first login of the day
                            (and only if "Show at first login of the day" is on)

Shows: clock + greeting · weather (Open-Meteo, location taken from the SimpleWeather top-bar
extension or ~/.config/bapirlo/location.json) · today's events from every calendar GNOME knows
(Evolution Data Server: Online Accounts → Google, local calendars, birthdays) · battery, CPU
temperature, power mode, storage, pending updates · HEALTH: battery wear, SSD SMART (wear, spare,
errors, hours, data written) and free space vs the 15 GB snapshot floor · FOCUS: today / this week /
streak from the top-bar focus timer's log, with a start/stop button · your dock favourites as quick launchers ·
Gaming / Quiet / Do Not Disturb switches (bapirlo-mode).

Cheap by design: nothing runs when the window is closed; network and calendar work happens in
threads; while open it refreshes sysfs readings every 5 s. It never wakes the NVIDIA GPU.
"""
